Revision history of trivnote-libexpr


0.1.0
    *** DataLoader.ParseException renamed to DataLoadingException
    *** DataLoader.eio() renamed to DataLoader.lastIOException()
    *** Walk renamed to DatumWalk (wherein tail renamed to rest)
    * Racket/Perl-ish "..." escapes!
    *-> |...| is now adorned with the same escapes.  this is
      NOT compatible with any Scheme-impl i know of!  if you
      want to remain compatible, you have to stick to simple
      un-escaped names or wait for a dedicated Scheme dumper...
    * DatumList as a real List<Datum>!
    *** Cons, Nil are no longer iterable; use Datum.asList.
    *** Cons is split into to two concrete types: the pairs
      (ConsCell) and the longer ones (ConsList as a singly
      linked list); use Cons.of instead of new Cons!  (Use
      Cons.ofList if you want an implicit Nil-terminator :)
    * AssocList as Map<Datum,Datum>!
    * Better Scalar hier
    * booleans?  (they're called TruthScalar for some reason.
      (not a reference to truth serum nuh-uh i don't do that))

0.0.0  2026-09-24  RC
    This was "done" a few days ago, but pinning this as a
    usable beta-ish version.

    - libexpr can represent s-expressions with cons cells/atoms.
      (( I respect Clojure/EDN, but i refuse to live without
         dotted pairs. :,> ))

    * libexpr can read s-expressions.  it understands symbols
      (interned in a symbol pool) and scalars (other strings).
      it is agnostic (in that the pool grows monotonically as
      it comes across anything that looks like a symbol), and is
      definitely vulnerable to DoS if there are too many symbols.
      (( That is the cost of not locking myself in to any
         specific vocabulary that i will reflect on later. ))
